silm:instances_papers_07_the_canonical_question_chapters_01_answerability_profile_sections_01_what_is_answerability_concrete_anchor_9#canonicalquestioncategory silm:hasLongDescription "The CanonicalQuestionCategory is O_07: the page-local canonical-question category with typed nodes, typed arrows, and the Node-or-Arrow admissibility gate. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol '\\C', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
